Z||000001||Robert||07-20-2000||07:33 PM||||I’ve had a cable modem for about 2 years now.  I was a Bata test site for the local cable company, (it sometimes pays to listen to those calls during dinner). Being a test site gave me free cable and Internet access for two months, BUT they still haven’t charged me.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I checked up on my account and I am listed as a vendor with complimentary service.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have seen the system slow down as more and more neighbors get online, but it’s still almost like working straight from the hard drive.<P>By the way....  we put in DSL service at the shop and it is even faster......<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 07-23-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||Raydar||07-21-2000||08:55 PM||||Well, I'm still waiting.<BR>The equipment that my cable company uses is the functional equivalent of two tin cans and a string. This, in suburban Atlanta.<BR>And, I live too far from the cental office to get DSL (at least until they find a way to make it run on fiber.)<BR>So, for now, I'm just screwed. Was hoping that Dish Network would come up with some sort of broadband. Even if it only supports downloads. Not happenin'. <BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
